{"version":"1.7","group":"V301","entries":[{"id":"learn:01810472-v","headword":"captivate","group":"V301","partOfSpeech":"verb","itemIds":["JBKROW008184","JBKROW011553"],"localGlosses":["(마음 따위를) 붙잡다"],"definitionEn":"attract; cause to be enamored","definitionKo":"마음을 끌어 매혹시키다","memoryKo":"시선과 마음을 붙잡아 놓아 다른 데로 돌리지 못하게 하는 장면을 떠올리세요.","usageKo":"이야기, 공연, 사람 등이 관심이나 마음을 강하게 사로잡는 문맥에 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"물리적으로 붙잡는 capture가 아니라 관심과 감정을 매혹해 사로잡는 뜻입니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"attract","noteKo":"attract가 관심을 끄는 일반 표현이라면 captivate는 관심을 강하게 붙들어 매혹한다는 느낌입니다."}],"example":{"en":"The opening scene captivated the audience.","ko":"첫 장면은 관객의 마음을 사로잡았다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/c/ca/captivate.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/c/ca/captivate.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"6c56850de0fcf6ca4c50a4561f5f5b0843c0e98cc5a699b6d44a413616f8591b"}]}},{"id":"learn:01764521-v","headword":"infatuate","group":"V301","partOfSpeech":"verb","itemIds":["JBKROW001538","JBKROW003008","JBKROW008187","JBKROW012385","JBKROW025612","JBKROW032062"],"localGlosses":["얼빠지게 만들다; 매혹하다"],"definitionEn":"arouse unreasoning love or passion in and cause to behave in an irrational way","definitionKo":"비이성적인 사랑이나 열정을 불러일으켜 이성을 잃게 하다","memoryKo":"강한 끌림 때문에 이성적 판단이 밀려나는 상태를 기억하세요.","usageKo":"사람이 누군가에게 맹목적이고 오래가지 않을 수 있는 강한 매혹을 느끼게 되는 문맥에 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"깊고 안정적인 love가 아니라 판단을 흐릴 만큼 비이성적인 열중이라는 점이 핵심입니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"love","noteKo":"love는 깊고 지속적인 애정을 포함할 수 있지만 infatuate는 맹목적이고 비이성적인 열광을 강조합니다."}],"example":{"en":"The celebrity's image infatuated many young fans.","ko":"그 유명인의 이미지는 많은 젊은 팬을 맹목적으로 매혹했다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/i/in/infatuate.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/i/in/infatuate.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"73eb32f7d9215491a6f2fd0d58f5d9627f014100a16b0e5747d14ca272b99035"}]}},{"id":"learn:07519226-n","headword":"revulsion","group":"V301","partOfSpeech":"noun","itemIds":["JBKROW008207","JBKROW013000","JBKROW024016","JBKROW026521","JBKROW027365","JBKROW029685","JBKROW033355"],"localGlosses":["(감정의 격변) 혐오; 불쾌"],"definitionEn":"intense aversion","definitionKo":"강렬한 혐오감","memoryKo":"보기만 해도 몸과 마음이 뒤로 물러나는 강한 거부감을 떠올리세요.","usageKo":"잔혹함, 부도덕함, 불쾌한 광경 등에 대한 매우 강한 혐오와 거부 반응을 나타낼 때 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"단순한 dislike보다 훨씬 강하며, 문맥에 따라 갑작스럽고 본능적인 혐오 반응을 나타냅니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"aversion","noteKo":"aversion은 강한 싫어함과 회피 성향을 넓게 뜻하고, revulsion은 몸서리칠 듯한 강렬한 혐오 반응을 강조합니다."}],"example":{"en":"He felt revulsion at the cruelty.","ko":"그는 그 잔혹함에 강한 혐오감을 느꼈다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/r/re/revulsion.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/r/re/revulsion.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"aa9b5144fc7a16c77964be4131283d71250af685d5a2fc9b7d16f874c8428dcb"}]}},{"id":"learn:00299633-a","headword":"cacophonous","group":"V301","partOfSpeech":"adjective","itemIds":["JBKROW004759","JBKROW006436","JBKROW008231","JBKROW010203","JBKROW011540","JBKROW024543","JBKROW028758","JBKROW030559"],"localGlosses":["불협화음의"],"definitionEn":"having an unpleasant sound","definitionKo":"불쾌한 소리를 내는","memoryKo":"서로 어울리지 않는 소리들이 부딪혀 귀를 괴롭히는 장면을 떠올리세요.","usageKo":"여러 소리가 뒤섞여 거칠고 듣기 불편한 상태를 묘사할 때 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"단순히 loud한 것이 아니라 소리의 결합이 거칠고 불쾌하다는 뜻입니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"dissonant","noteKo":"dissonant는 조화되지 않음을, cacophonous는 뒤섞인 소리 전체가 거칠고 불쾌함을 더 강하게 드러냅니다."}],"example":{"en":"A cacophonous mix of horns filled the street.","ko":"불협화음을 이루는 경적 소리가 거리를 가득 채웠다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/c/ca/cacophonous.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/c/ca/cacophonous.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"119391c76d76a1abcd9a2c0fd11b3b21fa46830d4964f23ba83d4cdbf10edf46"}]},"audio":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9f/En-us-cacophonous.ogg/En-us-cacophonous.ogg.mp3","region":"US","source":"Wikimedia Commons","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:En-us-cacophonous.ogg","license":"CC0","attribution":"0x0077BE"}},{"id":"learn:00770823-v","headword":"cajole","group":"V301","partOfSpeech":"verb","itemIds":["JBKROW005429","JBKROW006438","JBKROW008253","JBKROW008630","JBKROW011541","JBKROW028123"],"localGlosses":["감언이설로 설득하다"],"definitionEn":"influence or urge by gentle urging, caressing, or flattering","definitionKo":"다정한 재촉이나 애정 표현, 아첨으로 설득하다","memoryKo":"강요하지 않고 달콤한 말과 칭찬으로 상대의 마음을 움직이는 모습을 떠올리세요.","usageKo":"마지못해 하는 사람을 칭찬이나 약속으로 달래어 어떤 행동을 하게 만드는 문맥에 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"명령하거나 논리만으로 설득하는 것이 아니라 아첨과 달래기를 수단으로 삼는다는 점이 중요합니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"coax","noteKo":"둘 다 부드럽게 설득하지만 cajole은 특히 아첨이나 달콤한 약속을 이용한다는 뉘앙스가 강합니다."}],"example":{"en":"She cajoled him into joining the project.","ko":"그녀는 그를 달래고 구슬려 프로젝트에 참여시켰다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/c/ca/cajole.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/c/ca/cajole.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"10391eedd3a73c8ba4027b9c12bfa431893bfb4781a510dc712f4ab43bd35291"}]},"audio":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/df/En-us-cajole.ogg/En-us-cajole.ogg.mp3","region":"US","source":"Wikimedia Commons","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:En-us-cajole.ogg","license":"Public domain","attribution":"Dvortygirl"}}]}
